# systemd-sysusers declaration for the hyprav trusted-reader group
# (shipped as packaging/hyprav.sysusers, see #143) and the unprivileged
# scan-worker user (#103). Debian consumes
# the twin copy at debian/hyprav.sysusers via dh_installsysusers -
# both declare the same two lines, keep them in sync.
#
# The three IOC /proc entries are 0640; membership in this group is
# what lets a non-root desktop user read them via the GUI dashboard
# and unprivileged `avctl save`. Fields per sysusers.d(5):
# type / name / id / GECOS - "-" id means allocate a system uid/gid
# dynamically, so no per-machine gid bookkeeping is needed anywhere
# (the modprobe hook and apply-ioc-group.sh reference the group by
# name, never by number).
g hyprav - -
#
# hyprav-scan: the user avd's scan workers drop to when AVD_PRIVSEP=1
# (docs/privilege-separation.md). It owns nothing, has no login shell and
# no home, and is not in the hyprav group. `u` also creates a group of the
# same name. avd refuses to start with AVD_PRIVSEP=1 if it is missing.
u hyprav-scan - "HyprAV scan worker (avd privilege separation)" - /usr/sbin/nologin
